  "name": "ACTH STIMULATION TEST FOR 17-OH PROGESTERONE",
  "code": "1733",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"75\" data-end=\"100\">ACTH stimulation test</strong> for <strong data-start=\"105\" data-end=\"140\">17-hydroxyprogesterone (17-OHP)</strong> is primarily used to <strong data-start=\"162\" data-end=\"186\">diagnose or rule out</strong> <strong data-start=\"187\" data-end=\"227\">Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia (CAH)</strong> due to <strong data-start=\"235\" data-end=\"264\">21-hydroxylase deficiency</strong>, the most common form of CAH.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Form</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Description</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Classic CAH</strong></td>\n<td>Severe enzyme deficiency, usually presents in infancy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Non-classic CAH</strong></td>\n<td>Partial deficiency, often presents in adolescence/adulthood with symptoms like hirsutism, irregular menses, infertility</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1847\" data-end=\"1887\"><strong data-start=\"1851\" data-end=\"1887\">Clinical Indications for Testing</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1888\" data-end=\"2053\">\n<li data-start=\"1888\" data-end=\"1921\">\n<p data-start=\"1890\" data-end=\"1921\">Ambiguous genitalia in newborns</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1922\" data-end=\"1946\">\n<p data-start=\"1924\" data-end=\"1946\">Early onset of puberty</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1947\" data-end=\"1990\">\n<p data-start=\"1949\" data-end=\"1990\">Hirsutism or irregular periods in females</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1991\" data-end=\"2029\">\n<p data-start=\"1993\" data-end=\"2029\">Infertility or adrenal incidentaloma</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2030\" data-end=\"2053\">\n<p data-start=\"2032\" data-end=\"2053\">Family history of CAH</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"2060\" data-end=\"2079\"><strong data-start=\"2064\" data-end=\"2079\">Limitations</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2080\" data-end=\"2318\">\n<li data-start=\"2080\" data-end=\"2144\">\n<p data-start=\"2082\" data-end=\"2144\">Hormonal levels vary by age, time of day, and menstrual cycle.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2145\" data-end=\"2230\">\n<p data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2230\">Borderline results may require <strong data-start=\"2178\" data-end=\"2212\">genetic testing (CYP21A2 gene)</strong> for confirmation.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2231\" data-end=\"2318\">\n<p data-start=\"2233\" data-end=\"2318\">Other adrenal tests (e.g., cortisol, ACTH, androgens) may aid in full interpretation.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
